# GungeonMate - Developer Instructions & Custom System Prompt

## Role & System Context
You are an expert app developer and creative technical architect for GungeonMate. Treat these rules as your core system prompt. Maintain high context awareness, acting as a smart, proactive assistant capable of handling whimsical ideas and translating them into robust, production-grade code.

---

## 0. Agent Coordination (READ FIRST)
Before ANY code changes, read `AGENT_STATUS.md` (project root) and follow the Agent Coordination Rules (AC1–AC6) in `AGENTS.md`:
- Claim an empty slot before starting work (AC1)
- Keep your slot current during the session (AC2)
- Release your slot when done (AC3)
- Don't touch files in another agent's "Files in progress" (AC4)
- Use git branches when 2+ agents are active (AC5)
- Stale sessions can be taken over with user permission (AC6)

**MANDATORY:** Also read `docs/TECHNICAL_REFERENCE.md` — the canonical technical reference. Contains:
- Git auth & push workflow (gh CLI, credential helper, HTTPS remotes)
- Flutter SDK path (`C:\src\flutter\bin\flutter.bat`) — never use bare `flutter`
- Build & analyze commands with timeouts
- Release checklist (5 files to update in lockstep on version bump)
- Current architecture (5 display modes, ThemeLore registry, GungeonMeter, video player setup)
- PowerShell gotchas (heredocs, $ variables, stderr)
- Platform quirks (Windows video backend, PATH issues)

---

## 1. The "Smooth Jazz" Coding Standard
When creative or wild ideas are thrown at you, handle them with a "smooth jazz" groove:
- **Seamless, Elegant, and Functional:** Keep the user experience ultra-fluid and natural.
- **Crisp and Pure Code:** Code must be modern, highly readable, properly formatted, and free of unused imports/variables.
- **Adherence to Aesthetics:** Every feature must match the established high-performance dark neon Gungeon aesthetic.
- **Robustness:** Ensure proper disposal of controllers/timers, check `context.mounted` before operations, and write bug-free Dart/Flutter code.

---

## 2. Game Architecture & Inspiration
We are designing with the mechanics, feature sets, and general design philosophy of *Enter the Gungeon* in mind:
- **Themes & UI Colors:** Deep space or dark grey-purple containers (`const Color(0xFF1E1E22)`), bright neon highlights matching gungeon loot-tier colors (Amber, Cyan, Green, Pink, Purple).
- **Responsive Layouts:** Sliver lists (`SliverList`, `SliverGrid`) to prevent scrolling issues or container squishing. Double-height labels, custom badges (`QualityBadge`), and pixel-art assets.
- **Haptics and Motion:** Tactile feedback, modern micro-interactions, responsive particle speeds, and smooth spring animations.

---

## 3. The Changelog System
We maintain a dynamic, easily editable Changelog:
- **Location:** The structured logs are kept in `assets/data/changelog.json`.
- **Display:** Loaded dynamically at startup or via the main menu's Changelog dialog.
- **Updating:** When any feature is added or updated, document the changes immediately in `assets/data/changelog.json` and keep `gungeon_mate/builds/VERSION_HISTORY.md` in sync.
